# sample.catalog — a small shop wall for `nacs --assembly-report`.
#
# The grammar is the .patch reader's, grown record openers: `cutter <name>` /
# `holder <name>` open a record, keyword-value lines follow, the record closes
# at the next opener or end of file. `#` comments anywhere. All dimensions are
# ABSOLUTE mm — a catalog states real hardware. `modulus` is GPa and
# `compliance` is mm per kN at the nose; neither is a length, neither scales.
#
# This file is a SEARCH SPACE, never a gauging source: the report proposes an
# assembly, and the chosen tool's actuals still arrive by declaration in the
# .cam program.
#
# Two optional fields carry the V3 remainders: `type` on a cutter names which
# feeds-table row it looks up (default Endmill, which is what the stiffness
# model actually describes), and `grip lo..hi` on a holder states the shank
# diameters it can really hold.
#
# `flute_count` (V4) is the last field between a record and a COMPLETE tool
# line: a count, not a length, and the one thing K3's chip-load identity
# (F = RPM x z x f_z) cannot be evaluated without. It is optional like the
# rest — a record without it still declares, the declaration just cannot ask
# for `feed=derive`.

cutter 1/8-carbide
dia 3.175
flute_len 12.7
shank_dia 3.175
overall_len 38.1
modulus 600
flute_count 3
cost 18

cutter 1/4-carbide
dia 6.35
flute_len 19.05
shank_dia 6.35
overall_len 63.5
modulus 600
flute_count 4
cost 26

cutter 3/8-carbide
dia 9.525
flute_len 25.4
shank_dia 9.525
overall_len 76.2
modulus 600
flute_count 4
cost 38

# A necked reach tool: the relieved section buys clearance and costs bending.
cutter 1/4-reach
dia 6.35
flute_len 12.7
neck_dia 5.8
neck_len 25.4
shank_dia 6.35
overall_len 76.2
modulus 600
flute_count 3
cost 41

# A fat, stiff standard holder — the nose that never enters a pocket.
holder er32-standard
nose_dia 40.0
nose_len 22.0
body_dia 63.0
gauge_len 60.0
compliance 2.0
cost 120

# The slim extended nose this item exists to find: less nominal stiffness,
# but it follows the tool into an opening and shortens stickout.
holder slim-nose
nose_dia 14.0
nose_len 45.0
body_dia 50.0
gauge_len 90.0
compliance 3.5
# A slim extended nose is built around small collets: it reaches, but it
# cannot hold a 3/8 shank. `grip` is optional — er32-standard above declares
# none, so it still considers every cutter exactly as it always has.
grip 3.0..8.0
cost 260

# The wall's ball, and the reason it is here: a curved cavity is finished by a
# ball or not at all (`validate`: "Finish operation requires a Ballmill tool or
# a custom tool profile"), so a shop wall with no ball on it cannot answer a
# funnel at all. `type` is the field V3 gave the record; the shipped feeds
# table has no Ballmill row, so this cutter's rows report `rpm n/a` — the
# honest omission, per row, exactly where a reader can see which number is
# missing.
cutter 1/4-ball
dia 6.35
type Ballmill
flute_len 12.7
shank_dia 6.35
overall_len 63.5
modulus 600
flute_count 2
cost 33
